## 8. Clean Architecture

Follow `lib/features/profile/` as the canonical reference. Every new feature mirrors
its folder layout, dependency direction, and naming — do not invent parallel
patterns.

### 8.1 Feature Folder Structure

Each feature is self-contained under `lib/features/{feature_name}/`:

```text
lib/features/profile/
├── profile_injection.dart          # GetIt registration + BlocProvider list
├── data/
│   ├── datasources/                # HTTP / local I/O only
│   ├── models/                     # JSON parsing (extends domain entities)
│   └── repositories/               # ProfileRepositoryImpl
├── domain/
│   ├── entities/                   # Pure Dart types — no Flutter, no Dio
│   ├── repositories/               # ProfileRepository (abstract contract)
│   └── usecases/                   # One UseCase per operation + *Params
└── presentation/
    ├── controller/{operation}/     # *Cubit + *States (part file)
    ├── pages/                      # Screens (when added)
    └── widgets/                    # Feature-specific UI (when added)
```

- One **Cubit per user-facing operation** — not one god cubit for the whole feature.
- One **UseCase per repository method** — `GetStudentProfileUseCase`,
  `UpdateStudentProfileUseCase`, etc.
- Mirror operation names across layers: `get_student_profile` →
  `GetStudentProfileCubit` → `GetStudentProfileUseCase` → `getStudentProfile()`.

### 8.2 Layer Boundaries & Dependency Direction

Dependencies flow **inward only**:

```text
Presentation (Cubit, pages, widgets)
    ↓ depends on
Domain (UseCase → Repository interface → Entity)
    ↑ implemented by
Data (RepositoryImpl → DataSource → Model)
```

| Layer | Owns | Must NOT import |
|---|---|---|
| **Domain** | Entities, repository contracts, use cases, `*Params` | `data/`, `presentation/`, Flutter, Dio |
| **Data** | DataSource, models, repository impl, JSON/`AppException` | `presentation/` |
| **Presentation** | Cubits, states, pages, widgets | `data/` (never datasource or repo impl) |

```dart
// ❌ BAD: cubit reaches into the data layer — bypasses domain, untestable
class GetStudentProfileCubit extends Cubit<GetStudentProfileState> {
  Future<void> fGetStudentProfile() async {
    final response = await dioConsumer.get('/student/profile/edit'); // data layer leak
    emit(GetStudentProfileSuccessState(data: Student.fromJson(response)));
  }
}

// ✅ GOOD: cubit depends only on a domain use case
class GetStudentProfileCubit extends Cubit<GetStudentProfileState> {
  GetStudentProfileCubit(this.getStudentProfileUseCase)
      : super(const GetStudentProfileInitialState());

  final GetStudentProfileUseCase getStudentProfileUseCase;

  Future<void> fGetStudentProfile() async {
    emit(const GetStudentProfileLoadingState());
    final result = await getStudentProfileUseCase(NoParams());
    result.fold(
      (failure) => emit(GetStudentProfileErrorState(
        message: failure.message ?? Strings.pleaseTryAgainLater,
      )),
      (response) => emit(GetStudentProfileSuccessState(data: response.data)),
    );
  }
}
```

### 8.3 Where Logic Belongs

| Concern | Layer | Example (profile) |
|---|---|---|
| HTTP calls, status checks, `fromJson` | **DataSource** | `ProfileRemoteDataSourceImpl.getStudentProfile()` |
| `AppException` → `Failure` mapping | **Repository impl** | `ProfileRepositoryImpl` — `on AppException catch` → `Left` |
| Delegate to repository | **UseCase** | `GetStudentProfileUseCase.call()` → `repository.getStudentProfile()` |
| Request field mapping (`first_name`) | **`*Params.toJson()`** | `UpdateStudentProfileParams` in usecase file |
| Loading / success / error UI states | **Cubit** | `emit(Loading)` → `fold` → `emit(Success \| Error)` |
| Assembling UI args into `*Params` | **Cubit** | `fUpdateStudentProfile(...)` builds `UpdateStudentProfileParams` |
| Layout, theming, navigation triggers | **Widget / page** | `BlocConsumer` builder + listener only |

**Rule:** If it touches the network, parses JSON, or maps exceptions — it belongs in
**data**. If it decides what the UI should show next — it belongs in the **cubit**.
If it draws pixels — it belongs in a **widget**.

### 8.4 Don't Put Business Logic in Widgets

Widgets render state and dispatch actions. They never call APIs, parse JSON, or
decide success/failure.

```dart
// ❌ BAD: widget owns async work, validation, and error handling
class StudentProfileScreen extends StatefulWidget {
  @override
  State<StudentProfileScreen> createState() => _StudentProfileScreenState();
}

class _StudentProfileScreenState extends State<StudentProfileScreen> {
  Student? student;

  @override
  void initState() {
    super.initState();
    _loadProfile();
  }

  Future<void> _loadProfile() async {
    try {
      final response = await dioConsumer.get('/student/profile/edit');
      setState(() => student = Student.fromJson(response['data']));
    } catch (e) {
      showAppSnackBar(context: context, message: e.toString(), type: ToastType.error);
    }
  }

  @override
  Widget build(BuildContext context) => Text(student?.fullName ?? '');
}

// ✅ GOOD: widget listens to cubit state, dispatches via context.read
class StudentProfileScreen extends StatelessWidget {
  const StudentProfileScreen({super.key});

  @override
  Widget build(BuildContext context) {
    return BlocConsumer<GetStudentProfileCubit, GetStudentProfileState>(
      listener: (context, state) {
        if (state is GetStudentProfileErrorState) {
          showAppSnackBar(
            context: context,
            message: state.message,
            type: ToastType.error,
          );
        }
      },
      builder: (context, state) => switch (state) {
        GetStudentProfileLoadingState() => const Center(
          child: CircularProgressIndicator(),
        ),
        GetStudentProfileSuccessState(:final data) => StudentProfileBody(
          student: data!,
        ),
        _ => const SizedBox.shrink(),
      },
    );
  }
}

// Dispatch once on entry (route initState, screen wrapper, or button press):
context.read<GetStudentProfileCubit>().fGetStudentProfile();
```

- Use **`BlocConsumer`** when a screen needs both rebuild (builder) and side effects
  (listener — snackbars, navigation).
- Use **`BlocBuilder`** / **`BlocSelector`** when only UI rebuild is needed.
- Use **`context.read<Cubit>()`** to dispatch — never `await` network calls in widgets.

### 8.5 Cubit & State Conventions

Match the profile controller pattern exactly:

```dart
// get_student_profile_cubit.dart
part 'get_student_profile_states.dart';

class GetStudentProfileCubit extends Cubit<GetStudentProfileState> {
  // ...
  Future<void> fGetStudentProfile() async { /* f-prefix for all public actions */ }
}

// get_student_profile_states.dart
part of 'get_student_profile_cubit.dart';

sealed class GetStudentProfileState extends Equatable { /* ... */ }
final class GetStudentProfileInitialState extends GetStudentProfileState { /* ... */ }
final class GetStudentProfileLoadingState extends GetStudentProfileState { /* ... */ }
final class GetStudentProfileSuccessState extends GetStudentProfileState { /* ... */ }
final class GetStudentProfileErrorState extends GetStudentProfileState { /* ... */ }
```

- **`f` prefix** on cubit action methods: `fGetStudentProfile`, `fUpdateStudentProfile`.
- **Sealed states** with `Initial → Loading → Success | Error` — use exhaustive
  `switch` in builders.
- States live in a **`part` file** — import only the cubit, not the states file.
- Cubit holds **no mutable side-channel fields** — all UI-relevant data flows through
  `emit` and sealed states so `BlocBuilder` stays reliable.
- Register cubits as **`registerFactory`** (new instance per provider scope).

### 8.6 Domain & Data Patterns

**UseCase** — thin delegate to repository. Do not add orchestration here unless the
feature genuinely needs multi-repository coordination.

```dart
class GetStudentProfileUseCase extends UseCase<GetStudentProfileResponse, NoParams> {
  final ProfileRepository repository;
  GetStudentProfileUseCase({required this.repository});

  @override
  Future<Either<Failure, GetStudentProfileResponse>> call(NoParams params) async {
    return await repository.getStudentProfile(params: params);
  }
}
```

**Repository impl** — catch `AppException`, return `Either`:

```dart
@override
Future<Either<Failure, GetStudentProfileResponse>> getStudentProfile({
  required NoParams params,
}) async {
  try {
    final response = await remote.getStudentProfile();
    return Right(response);
  } on AppException catch (error) {
    Log.e('[getStudentProfile] [${error.runtimeType}] ---- ${error.message}');
    return Left(error.toFailure());
  }
}
```

**Model** — extends entity, adds `fromJson`. No separate mapper class unless parsing
logic is genuinely complex:

```dart
class GetStudentProfileModel extends GetStudentProfileResponse {
  factory GetStudentProfileModel.fromJson(Map<String, dynamic> json) =>
      GetStudentProfileModel(
        status: json['status'] ?? '',
        message: json['message'] ?? '',
        data: StudentModel.fromJson(json['data']),
      );
}
```

**DataSource** — owns endpoints and raw HTTP. Throws `ServerException` on failure:

```dart
Future<GetStudentProfileModel> getStudentProfile() async {
  const endpoint = '/student/profile/edit';
  final response = await dioConsumer.get(endpoint);
  if (response['status'] == 'success') {
    return GetStudentProfileModel.fromJson(response);
  }
  throw ServerException(message: response['message'] ?? '');
}
```

- Co-locate **`*Params`** with their use case file; include `toJson()` for request
  bodies — this is the existing project convention.
- Return **`Either<Failure, T>`** end-to-end from repository through use case to cubit.

### 8.7 Dependency Injection

Every feature exposes `{feature}_injection.dart` following profile:

```dart
Future<void> initProfileFeatureInjection() async {
  // Cubits — registerFactory
  _sl.registerFactory<GetStudentProfileCubit>(() => GetStudentProfileCubit(_sl()));

  // UseCases — registerLazySingleton
  _sl.registerLazySingleton<GetStudentProfileUseCase>(
    () => GetStudentProfileUseCase(repository: _sl()),
  );

  // Repository — registerLazySingleton
  _sl.registerLazySingleton<ProfileRepository>(
    () => ProfileRepositoryImpl(remote: _sl()),
  );

  // DataSource — registerLazySingleton
  _sl.registerLazySingleton<ProfileRemoteDataSource>(
    () => ProfileRemoteDataSourceImpl(),
  );
}

List<BlocProvider> get profileBlocs => <BlocProvider>[
  BlocProvider<GetStudentProfileCubit>(
    create: (context) => _sl<GetStudentProfileCubit>(),
  ),
  // ...one BlocProvider per cubit
];
```

- Call `init{Feature}FeatureInjection()` from `injection_container.dart`.
- Spread `...{feature}Blocs` into `MultiBlocProvider` in `app.dart`.
- **Never** construct cubits, use cases, or repositories with `new` in widgets.

### 8.8 Avoid Unnecessary Abstractions

Follow profile's pragmatic style — add layers only when they solve a real problem:

| Don't add | Why — profile already handles it |
|---|---|
| Separate mapper classes | Models extend entities with `fromJson` |
| Service layer between cubit and use case | Cubit → UseCase is sufficient |
| One god cubit per feature | One cubit per operation scales and tests cleanly |
| Extra repository interfaces per operation | One `{Feature}Repository` with focused methods |
| Generic `BaseCubit` / `BaseRepository` wrappers | Repeat the proven pattern; don't abstract prematurely |
| Domain events / command buses | Cubit `f*` methods are the dispatch mechanism |

**Do add** a new use case + cubit + datasource method when the operation is a
distinct user action or API endpoint — that is the expected unit of decomposition,
not over-engineering.

### 8.9 Quick Checklist

| Check | Pass criteria |
|---|---|
| Feature folder matches profile layout | `data/`, `domain/`, `presentation/controller/` |
| Domain imports nothing from data/presentation | No Flutter, Dio, or `*_model.dart` |
| Cubit imports only use cases + entities | No datasource, no repo impl |
| Widgets dispatch via `context.read<Cubit>().f…()` | No `dioConsumer`, no `setState` for API data |
| Errors flow as `Either<Failure, T>` | Exceptions caught only in repository impl |
| DI registered in `{feature}_injection.dart` | Factory for cubits, lazy singleton for rest |
| States are sealed + `part of` cubit | `Initial / Loading / Success / Error` |

